<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{ title }}</title>
</head>
<body>

<section class="title-page" style="page: title;">
  <div class="title-band"></div>
  <h1 class="report-title">{{ title }}</h1>
  <p class="report-subtitle">Threat Model Report</p>
  <hr class="title-rule">
  <table class="title-meta">
    <tr><th>Date</th><td>{{ date }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Author</th><td>{{ author.get('name', '') }}{% if author.get('role') %} ({{ author.role }}){% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Mission Criticality</th><td>{{ mission_criticality }}</td></tr>
  </table>
</section>

<section class="toc" style="page: toc;">
  <h1>Table of Contents</h1>
  <ul class="toc-list">
    <li class="toc-l0"><a href="#methodology">Part I: Application Profile</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#methodology"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#methodology">Threagile Methodology</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#methodology"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#executive-summary">Executive Summary</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#executive-summary"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#data-flow-diagram">Data-Flow Diagram</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#data-flow-diagram"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#data-asset-diagram">Data Asset Diagram</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#data-asset-diagram"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#application-features">Application Features and Scoping</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#application-features"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#security-requirements">Security Requirements and Abuse Cases</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#security-requirements"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#model-failures">Potential Model Failures</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#model-failures"></a></li>

    <li class="toc-l0"><a href="#impact-methodology">Part II: Application Risks</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#impact-methodology"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#impact-methodology">Risk Methodology</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#impact-methodology"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#impact-analysis">Severity Analysis of {{ remaining_finding_count }} Open Risks in {{ remaining_categories | length }} Categories</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#impact-analysis"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#accepted-risks">Severity Analysis of {{ accepted_finding_count }} Accepted Risks in {{ accepted_categories | length }} Categories</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#accepted-risks"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#closed-risks">Severity Analysis of {{ closed_finding_count }} Closed Risks in {{ closed_categories | length }} Categories</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#closed-risks"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#risks-by-category">Identified Risks by Vulnerability Category</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#risks-by-category"></a></li>
    {% for group in all_domain_groups %}
    <li class="toc-l2"><a href="#domain-{{ group.slug }}">{{ group.domain }}</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#domain-{{ group.slug }}"></a></li>
    {% endfor %}

    <li class="toc-l0"><a href="#data-assets">Part III: Application Components</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#data-assets"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#data-assets">Data Assets</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#data-assets"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#technical-assets">Technical Assets</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#technical-assets"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#out-of-scope-assets">Out of Scope Assets</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#out-of-scope-assets"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#trust-boundaries">Trust Boundaries</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#trust-boundaries"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#shared-runtimes">Shared Runtimes</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#shared-runtimes"></a></li>
    <li class="toc-l1"><a href="#disclaimer">Disclaimer</a><span class="toc-fill"></span><a class="toc-page" href="#disclaimer"></a></li>
  </ul>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- PART 1: APPLICATION PROFILE                                  -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->

<section id="methodology" style="page: content;">
  <h1>Part I: Application Profile</h1>
  <h2 class="section-heading">Threagile Methodology</h2>
  <p>This report was produced with <strong>Threagile</strong>, an open-source, model-driven threat
  modeling engine. The system's architecture, technical assets, trust boundaries, data flows, and
  data assets are described as structured data rather than drawn by hand. Threagile then analyzes
  that model against a library of risk rules, which shows where the architecture does not meet the
  expected security properties. Additionally, this model's custom risk-injection engine extends that
  analysis with risk categories built for this organization's compliance and hardening
  requirements.</p>
</section>

<section id="executive-summary" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Executive Summary</h2>
  <p>This section covers what the system does, how it is built, and where its identified risks stand.</p>

  <h2>Mission Criticality</h2>
  <p>This model is rated <strong>{{ mission_criticality }}</strong>. The rating changes no finding's
  score. However, at Mission Essential or above, the incident-response readiness checks (IR plan
  testing, breach notification, forensic chain of custody, and containment disposition) apply to the
  model's assets.</p>
  <table class="asset-table">
    <tr><th>Level</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
    {% for level, meaning in [
      ("Administrative", "Supports administrative or back-office functions. The mission continues without it."),
      ("Mission Support", "Supports the mission. Loss degrades it, but workarounds exist."),
      ("Mission Essential", "Needed to accomplish the mission. Loss stops a mission function."),
      ("Mission Critical", "Warfighting or core operational system. Loss causes immediate mission failure."),
    ] %}
    {% if level == mission_criticality %}
    <tr><td><strong>{{ level }} (this model)</strong></td><td><strong>{{ meaning }}</strong></td></tr>
    {% else %}
    <tr><td>{{ level }}</td><td>{{ meaning }}</td></tr>
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </table>

  <h2>Application Overview</h2>
  <p>{{ management_summary_comment }}</p>

  <table class="summary-counts">
    <tr>
      <th>Severity</th>
      {% for status in ['unchecked', 'in-progress', 'in-discussion', 'mitigated', 'accepted', 'false-positive'] %}
      <th>{{ status | replace('-', ' ') | capitalize }}</th>
      {% endfor %}
      <th>Total</th>
    </tr>
    {% for sev in severity_order %}
    {% set by_status = stats.get(sev, {}) %}
    <tr>
      <td class="severity-{{ sev }}">{{ sev | capitalize }}</td>
      {% for status in ['unchecked', 'in-progress', 'in-discussion', 'mitigated', 'accepted', 'false-positive'] %}
      <td>{{ by_status.get(status, 0) }}</td>
      {% endfor %}
      <td>{{ by_status.values() | sum }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>

  {% if threat_landscape.description %}
  <h2>Threat Landscape</h2>
  {% for para in threat_landscape.description.split('\n') if para.strip() %}<p>{{ para.strip() }}</p>{% endfor %}
  {% endif %}
  {% if technical_overview.description %}
  <h2>Technical Overview</h2>
  {% for para in technical_overview.description.split('\n') if para.strip() %}<p>{{ para.strip() }}</p>{% endfor %}
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section id="data-flow-diagram" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Data-Flow Diagram</h2>
  <p>This diagram shows every technical asset, trust boundary, and communication link in the
  application model. Small icons in the corner of a node or boundary mark specific application
  components or cloud services where they are tagged. This page is a fixed-size
  overview, while the accompanying <code>data-flow-diagram.html</code> (or <code>.svg</code>) file is
  a full-resolution, zoomable version.</p>
  <div class="diagram">{{ data_flow_diagram | safe }}</div>
</section>

<section id="data-asset-diagram" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Data Asset Diagram</h2>
  <p>This diagram maps each data asset to every technical asset that sends, receives, or stores it.
  Both kinds of asset are shaded by their Confidentiality level (see Data Assets). A solid edge means
  the technical asset stores the data asset, whereas a dashed edge means the data asset is processed
  by or passes through that asset without being stored there. This page is a fixed-size overview,
  while the accompanying <code>data-asset-diagram.html</code> (or <code>.svg</code>) file is a
  full-resolution, zoomable version.</p>
  <div class="diagram">{{ data_asset_diagram | safe }}</div>
</section>

<section id="application-features" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Application Features and Scoping</h2>
  <p>This section establishes which features the application has, and therefore which of the
  security requirements in the next section apply. It has two parts. First, the feature checklist
  records facts that no tag or model field captures, such as whether any local accounts exist. It
  shows the options selected for each item, and it lists the requirement sections each item affects and the tags
  and model fields its selections imply. A reviewer checks that each implied tag and field appears on
  the asset that has the feature. Where an answer rules out a section, the next section shows it as
  not applicable, with the reason.</p>
  <p>Second, the questions explain how each capability the application has is implemented and
  verified. A question that the checklist rules out is left out, and a question that depends on an
  unanswered checklist item appears as pending. Both parts are grouped by the same focus areas as the
  requirements, and any entry without a focus area falls under Uncategorized.</p>
  {% if feature_checklist %}
  <h2 class="domain-heading">Feature Checklist</h2>
  <table class="asset-table feature-checklist">
    <tr><th>Focus Area</th><th>Feature</th><th>Selection</th><th>Sections affected, and implied tags and fields</th></tr>
    {% for row in feature_checklist %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ row.domain }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.feature }}{% if not row.multiple %} <span class="select-note">(select one)</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td>
        {% for option in row.options if option.selected %}<div class="opt on"><span class="box checked"></span>{{ option.label }}</div>{% endfor %}
        {% for extra in row.unknown %}<div class="opt on"><span class="box checked"></span>{{ extra }}</div>{% endfor %}
        {% if not row.answered %}<div class="opt-flag">Not answered</div>{% endif %}
        {% if row.confirm %}<div class="opt-flag">To be confirmed</div>{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>{{ row.affects or '—' }}{% for tag in row.tags %}<div class="implied-tag">{{ tag }}</div>{% endfor %}{% for field in row.fields %}<div class="implied-field">{{ field }}</div>{% endfor %}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}
  {% for group in question_domain_groups %}
  <h2 class="domain-heading">{{ group.domain }}</h2>
  {% for q_title, q_text in group.entries %}
  <h3 class="category-heading">{{ q_title }}</h3>
  {% for para in (q_text or '').split('\n') if para.strip() %}<p>{{ para.strip() }}</p>{% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% for entry in group.absent %}
  <h3 class="category-heading question-absent">{{ entry.question }}</h3>
  {% if entry.status == 'pending' %}<p class="question-note">Pending: {{ entry.reason }}.</p>
  {% else %}<p class="question-note missing">Not answered: this question applies to the model but has no answer.</p>{% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="security-requirements" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Security Requirements and Abuse Cases</h2>
  <p>This section covers the mandatory controls and constraints for the application model, drawn
  from OWASP ASVS and AISVS or NIST SP 800-53 and grouped by focus area. Where an abuse case describes
  an attacker goal that a requirement answers, it appears above that requirement's table, and abuse
  cases that no requirement in this model answers are listed at the end of their focus area.
  Additionally, requirement sections that the application's features rule out are marked not
  applicable, with the reason ({{ not_applicable_requirement_count }} in this model). Any tailored
  entry that does not belong to a focus area falls under Uncategorized.</p>
  {% for group in requirement_abuse_groups %}
  <h2 class="domain-heading">{{ group.domain }}</h2>
  {% for req in group.entries %}
  <h3 class="category-heading">{{ req.title }}</h3>
  {% for ac_title, ac_text in req.abuse_cases %}
  <div class="abuse-callout">
    <div class="ac-label">Abuse case</div>
    <div class="ac-title">{{ ac_title.split(':', 1)[-1].strip() }}</div>
    <p>{{ ac_text }}</p>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  {% if req.not_applicable %}
  <p class="req-not-applicable"><strong>Not applicable:</strong> {{ req.not_applicable }}</p>
  {% elif req.rows %}
  <table class="svs-table">
    <thead><tr><th class="svs-num">#</th><th>Description</th><th class="svs-level">Level</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in req.rows %}
      <tr><td class="svs-num">{{ row.num }}</td><td>{{ row.description }}</td><td class="svs-level level-{{ row.level }}">{{ row.level }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% else %}
  <p>{{ req.text }}</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% if group.unmapped %}
  <div class="abuse-unmapped">
    <h3 class="category-heading">Abuse cases without a mapped requirement</h3>
    <p class="abuse-unmapped-note">No requirement section in this model answers these attacker goals.</p>
    {% for ac_title, ac_text in group.unmapped %}
    <div class="abuse-callout gap">
      <div class="ac-title">{{ ac_title }}</div>
      <p>{{ ac_text }}</p>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
</section>


<section id="model-failures" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Potential Model Failures</h2>
  <p>This section lists the findings from Threagile's model-consistency rules, such as unreferenced
  or unnecessary assets and incomplete boundary or link content. These findings do not indicate an
  architecture risk. Instead, they flag problems in how the model was authored, so the fix is to
  correct the model rather than to add mitigating controls.</p>
  {% if model_failure_categories %}
  {% for cat in model_failure_categories %}
  <h2>{{ cat.title }}</h2>
  {% for f in cat.findings %}
  <div class="finding">
    <h3><span class="severity-badge severity-{{ f.severity }}">{{ f.severity | upper }}</span> {{ f.title }}</h3>
    <p><strong>Asset:</strong> {{ f.most_relevant_technical_asset or '—' }}</p>
    {% if f.action %}<p><strong>Action:</strong> {{ f.action | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
    {% if f.mitigation %}<p><strong>Mitigation:</strong> {{ f.mitigation | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% else %}
  <p>No model-failure findings in this run.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- PART 2: APPLICATION RISKS                                    -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->

<section id="impact-methodology" style="page: content;">
  <h1>Part II: Application Risks</h1>
  <h2 class="section-heading">Risk Methodology</h2>
  <p>Every finding receives a Severity on a five-level scale,
  <span class="severity-low">Low</span> &lt; <span class="severity-medium">Medium</span> &lt;
  <span class="severity-elevated">Elevated</span> &lt; <span class="severity-high">High</span> &lt;
  <span class="severity-critical">Critical</span>. Each finding starts from a baseline Likelihood and
  Impact set by its rule. The baseline is then tailored to the asset that the finding lands on, based
  on (1) how attractive the asset is to an attacker, (2) whether it can be reached from the internet,
  and (3) how the asset is rated on the security property that the threat endangers (confidentiality,
  integrity, or availability). Finally, the tailored Likelihood and Impact combine into a Severity, as
  shown below.</p>
  <table class="severity-matrix">
    <caption>Severity matrix (rows are Likelihood, columns are Impact)</caption>
    <tr><th></th><th>Low (1)</th><th>Medium (2)</th><th>High (3)</th><th>Very-High (5)</th></tr>
    <tr><th>Unlikely (1)</th><td class="severity-low">Low</td><td class="severity-medium">Medium</td><td class="severity-medium">Medium</td><td class="severity-elevated">Elevated</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Possible (2)</th><td class="severity-medium">Medium</td><td class="severity-elevated">Elevated</td><td class="severity-elevated">Elevated</td><td class="severity-high">High</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Likely (3)</th><td class="severity-medium">Medium</td><td class="severity-elevated">Elevated</td><td class="severity-high">High</td><td class="severity-high">High</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Very-Likely (5)</th><td class="severity-elevated">Elevated</td><td class="severity-high">High</td><td class="severity-high">High</td><td class="severity-critical">Critical</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p>For further details, see the program's Application Risk Methodology.</p>
</section>

{% macro severity_summary(groups) %}
  <table class="compact-risk-table severity-summary">
    <tr><th>Category</th>{% for sev in severity_order %}<th>{{ sev | capitalize }}</th>{% endfor %}<th>Total</th></tr>
    {% for group in groups %}
    <tr class="summary-domain"><td colspan="{{ severity_order | length + 2 }}">{{ group.domain }}</td></tr>
    {% for cat in group.categories %}
    <tr>
      <td><a href="#cat-{{ cat.slug }}">{{ cat.title }}</a></td>
      {% for sev in severity_order %}{% set n = cat.findings | selectattr('severity', 'equalto', sev) | list | length %}<td{% if n %} class="severity-{{ sev }}"{% endif %}>{{ n if n else '' }}</td>{% endfor %}
      <td>{{ cat.findings | length }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
{% endmacro %}

<section id="impact-analysis" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Severity Analysis of {{ remaining_finding_count }} Open Risks in {{ remaining_categories | length }} Categories</h2>
  <p>This section covers open risks, which are the findings marked unchecked, in progress, or in
  discussion. These risks have been neither mitigated nor accepted.</p>
  <p>Open risks are split by what the threat model can show. <strong>Model Weaknesses</strong>
  ({{ remaining_weakness_finding_count }}) are findings that the model's own facts demonstrate, such
  as data sent over a plain-HTTP link or a static secret used to authenticate.
  <strong>Control Verifications</strong> ({{ remaining_control_finding_count }}) are findings raised
  because an interface or capability exists, while the model cannot show whether the control is in
  place. A reviewer confirms each one, and its Severity is the rating that applies if the control
  turns out to be missing.</p>

  <p>Each table counts a category's open findings by Severity, and each category links to its full
  detail under Identified Risks by Vulnerability Category.</p>

  <h2 class="domain-heading">Model Weaknesses ({{ remaining_weakness_finding_count }})</h2>
  {% if remaining_weakness_domain_groups %}{{ severity_summary(remaining_weakness_domain_groups) }}
  {% else %}<p>No open model weaknesses.</p>{% endif %}

  <h2 class="domain-heading">Control Verifications ({{ remaining_control_finding_count }})</h2>
  {% if remaining_control_domain_groups %}{{ severity_summary(remaining_control_domain_groups) }}
  {% else %}<p>No open control verifications.</p>{% endif %}

  {% if remaining_unclassified_finding_count %}
  <h2 class="domain-heading">Other Open Risks ({{ remaining_unclassified_finding_count }})</h2>
  <p>Findings from rules that carry no finding class.</p>
  {{ severity_summary(remaining_unclassified_domain_groups) }}
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section id="accepted-risks" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Severity Analysis of {{ accepted_finding_count }} Accepted Risks in {{ accepted_categories | length }} Categories</h2>
  <p>This section covers accepted risks, which are findings whose vulnerability is still present in
  the architecture, but which a documented decision tolerates rather than remediates. Each acceptance
  records a justification, a ticket reference, a reviewer, and a date.</p>
  {% if accepted_categories %}
  {% for group in accepted_domain_groups %}
  <h2 class="domain-heading">{{ group.domain }}</h2>
  {% for cat in group.categories %}
  <h3 class="category-heading"><a href="#cat-{{ cat.slug }}">{{ cat.title }}</a></h3>
  <table class="compact-risk-table">
    <tr><th>Severity</th><th>Asset</th><th>Justification</th><th>Ticket</th><th>Checked By</th><th>Date</th></tr>
    {% for f in cat.findings %}
    <tr>
      <td class="severity-{{ f.severity }}">{{ f.severity | capitalize }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.most_relevant_technical_asset or '—' }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.justification or '—' }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.ticket or '—' }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.checked_by or '—' }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.closed_date or '—' }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% else %}
  <p>No accepted risks in this run.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section id="closed-risks" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Severity Analysis of {{ closed_finding_count }} Closed Risks in {{ closed_categories | length }} Categories</h2>
  <p>This section covers closed risks, which are the mitigated and false-positive findings. In these,
  the vulnerability is either fixed or was never a real exposure. Each one has a justification, a
  reviewer, and a date from its <code>risk_tracking</code> entry.</p>
  {% if closed_categories %}
  {% for group in closed_domain_groups %}
  <h2 class="domain-heading">{{ group.domain }}</h2>
  {% for cat in group.categories %}
  <h3 class="category-heading"><a href="#cat-{{ cat.slug }}">{{ cat.title }}</a></h3>
  <table class="compact-risk-table">
    <tr><th>Severity</th><th>Asset</th><th>Status</th><th>Justification</th><th>Checked By</th><th>Date</th></tr>
    {% for f in cat.findings %}
    <tr>
      <td class="severity-{{ f.severity }}">{{ f.severity | capitalize }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.most_relevant_technical_asset or '—' }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.risk_status | replace('-', ' ') | capitalize }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.justification or '—' }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.checked_by or '—' }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.closed_date or '—' }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% else %}
  <p>No closed risks in this run.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section id="risks-by-category" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Identified Risks by Vulnerability Category</h2>
  <p>This section gives the full detail of every finding, grouped by focus area. Each category's
  detection logic, false positives, and risk assessment are in the program's Threat Catalogue.</p>
  {% for group in all_domain_groups %}
  <h2 id="domain-{{ group.slug }}" class="domain-heading">{{ group.domain }}</h2>
  {% for cat in group.categories %}
  <div id="cat-{{ cat.slug }}" class="category-block">

    {% if cat.shared %}
    {# Every finding in this category shares its STRIDE, function, CWE, action, and mitigation, so
       those are shown once. Severity, likelihood, impact, and status stay per asset in the table, so
       that every category has the same shape. #}
    <div class="finding">
      <h3 class="category-heading">{{ cat.title }}</h3>
      <table class="finding-meta">
        <tr>
          <td><strong>STRIDE:</strong> {{ cat.shared.stride }}</td>
          <td><strong>Function:</strong> {{ cat.shared.function }}</td>
          <td><strong>CWE:</strong> {{ cat.shared.cwe }}</td>
          {% if cat.finding_class_label %}<td><strong>Finding class:</strong> {{ cat.finding_class_label }}</td>{% endif %}
        </tr>
      </table>
      <table class="compact-risk-table">
        <tr><th>Severity</th><th>Asset</th><th>Communication Link</th><th>Likelihood</th><th>Impact Rating</th><th>Status</th></tr>
        {% for f in cat.findings %}
        <tr id="finding-{{ f.synthetic_id }}">
          <td class="severity-{{ f.severity }}">{{ f.severity | capitalize }}</td>
          <td>{{ f.most_relevant_technical_asset or '—' }}</td>
          <td>{{ f.communication_link or '—' }}</td>
          <td>{{ f.exploitation_likelihood | capitalize }}</td>
          <td>{{ f.exploitation_impact | capitalize }}</td>
          <td>{{ f.risk_status | replace('-', ' ') | capitalize }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table>
      {% if cat.enrichment %}
      <p><strong>Description:</strong> {{ cat.enrichment.description }}</p>
      <p><strong>Impact:</strong> {{ cat.enrichment.impact }}</p>
      {% endif %}
      {% if cat.shared.action %}<p><strong>Action:</strong> {{ cat.shared.action | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if cat.shared.mitigation %}<p><strong>Mitigation:</strong> {{ cat.shared.mitigation | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if cat.enrichment %}
      {% if cat.enrichment.asvs %}<p><strong>ASVS:</strong> {{ cat.enrichment.asvs }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if cat.enrichment.cheat_sheet %}<p><strong>Cheat Sheet:</strong> {{ cat.enrichment.cheat_sheet }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if cat.enrichment.references %}<p><strong>References:</strong> {{ cat.enrichment.references }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% else %}
    {# The findings disagree on STRIDE, function, CWE, action, or mitigation, so each keeps its own
       block. Only the first carries the category heading and description. #}
    {% for f in cat.findings %}
    <div id="finding-{{ f.synthetic_id }}" class="finding">
      <h3{% if loop.first %} class="category-heading"{% endif %}>{{ f.title }}</h3>
      <table class="finding-meta">
        <tr>
          <td><strong>STRIDE:</strong> {{ f.stride }}</td>
          <td><strong>Function:</strong> {{ f.function }}</td>
          <td><strong>CWE:</strong> {{ f.cwe }}</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <table class="compact-risk-table">
        <tr><th>Severity</th><th>Asset</th><th>Communication Link</th><th>Likelihood</th><th>Impact Rating</th><th>Status</th></tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="severity-{{ f.severity }}">{{ f.severity | capitalize }}</td>
          <td>{{ f.most_relevant_technical_asset or '—' }}</td>
          <td>{{ f.communication_link or '—' }}</td>
          <td>{{ f.exploitation_likelihood | capitalize }}</td>
          <td>{{ f.exploitation_impact | capitalize }}</td>
          <td>{{ f.risk_status | replace('-', ' ') | capitalize }}</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      {% if loop.first and cat.enrichment %}
      <p><strong>Description:</strong> {{ cat.enrichment.description }}</p>
      <p><strong>Impact:</strong> {{ cat.enrichment.impact }}</p>
      {% endif %}
      {% if f.action %}<p><strong>Action:</strong> {{ f.action | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if f.mitigation %}<p><strong>Mitigation:</strong> {{ f.mitigation | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if loop.first and cat.enrichment %}
      {% if cat.enrichment.asvs %}<p><strong>ASVS:</strong> {{ cat.enrichment.asvs }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if cat.enrichment.cheat_sheet %}<p><strong>Cheat Sheet:</strong> {{ cat.enrichment.cheat_sheet }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if cat.enrichment.references %}<p><strong>References:</strong> {{ cat.enrichment.references }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
</section>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- PART 3: APPLICATION COMPONENTS                                -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->

<section id="data-assets" style="page: content;">
  <h1>Part III: Application Components</h1>
  <h2 class="section-heading">Data Assets</h2>
  <p>This section outlines the information that the application model processes or stores,
  regardless of which technical asset handles it. Each entry records who is accountable for it
  (<strong>Owner</strong>), roughly how much of it exists (<strong>Quantity</strong>), where it comes
  from (<strong>Origin</strong>), and its Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability ratings, which
  are defined below.</p>

  <h2>Confidentiality</h2>
  <table class="asset-table">
    <tr><th>Level</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Public</td><td>No confidentiality requirement. Freely shareable.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Internal</td><td>Internal to the organization. Not for public release.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Restricted</td><td>Limited distribution within the organization. Need-to-know basis.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Confidential</td><td>Sensitive business or personal data. Restricted by policy.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Strictly-Confidential</td><td>Highest sensitivity. CUI, classified, or regulated data.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Integrity &amp; Availability</h2>
  <p>Integrity and Availability share one five-level scale, which rates what happens if the asset is
  modified (Integrity) or made unavailable (Availability). Technical Assets (the next section) uses
  the same scale, applied to the asset itself rather than to a specific payload.</p>
  <table class="asset-table">
    <tr><th>Level</th><th>If modified (Integrity)</th><th>If unavailable (Availability)</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Archive</td><td>Historical/reference data. Modification has minimal impact.</td><td>Minimal operational impact.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Operational</td><td>Operational data. Modification causes limited disruption.</td><td>Causes limited disruption.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Important</td><td>Important data. Modification causes significant disruption.</td><td>Causes significant disruption.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Critical</td><td>Critical data. Modification causes major mission impact.</td><td>Causes major mission impact.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Mission-Critical</td><td>Modification causes immediate mission failure.</td><td>Causes immediate mission failure.</td></tr>
  </table>

  {% for a in data_assets %}
  <div class="asset-node">
    <h3>{{ a.title }}</h3>
    <table class="finding-meta">
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Owner:</strong> {{ a.owner }}</td>
        <td><strong>Quantity:</strong> {{ a.quantity }}</td>
        <td><strong>Origin:</strong> {{ a.origin }}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Confidentiality:</strong> <span class="cia-badge conf-{{ a.confidentiality }}">{{ a.confidentiality }}</span></td>
        <td><strong>Integrity:</strong> <span class="cia-badge ia-{{ a.integrity }}">{{ a.integrity }}</span></td>
        <td><strong>Availability:</strong> <span class="cia-badge ia-{{ a.availability }}">{{ a.availability }}</span></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    {% if a.description %}<p>{{ a.description }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="technical-assets" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Technical Assets</h2>
  <p>This section describes every component in the application model's architecture, with its
  risk-relevant attributes: <strong>Type</strong> (external-entity, process, or datastore),
  <strong>Technology</strong> (its technical classification), <strong>Machine</strong> (physical,
  virtual, container, or serverless), and <strong>Encryption</strong>. Confidentiality, Integrity, and
  Availability use the scale defined in Data Assets, applied to the asset itself rather than to a
  specific payload.</p>
  <p>Relative Attacker Attractiveness (RAA) is a score that Threagile computes for each asset from its
  exposure, size, and CIA ratings, and it estimates how appealing a target the asset is relative to
  the rest of the model. Both rule sources use RAA in their likelihood scoring, so it helps explain
  why some findings are rated more severely than others.</p>
  {% macro raa_badge(raa) -%}
  {%- if raa is none -%}
  —
  {%- else -%}
  {%- set band = 'critical' if raa >= 80 else 'high' if raa >= 60 else 'elevated' if raa >= 40 else 'medium' if raa >= 20 else 'low' -%}
  <span class="raa-badge raa-{{ band }}">{{ raa | round | int }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- endmacro %}
  {% for a in technical_assets %}
  <div class="asset-node">
    <h3>{{ a.title }}</h3>
    <table class="finding-meta">
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Type:</strong> {{ a.type }}</td>
        <td><strong>Technology:</strong> {{ a.technology }}</td>
        <td><strong>Machine:</strong> {{ a.machine }}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Encryption:</strong> {{ a.encryption }}</td>
        <td><strong>Confidentiality:</strong> <span class="cia-badge conf-{{ a.confidentiality }}">{{ a.confidentiality }}</span></td>
        <td><strong>Integrity:</strong> <span class="cia-badge ia-{{ a.integrity }}">{{ a.integrity }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Availability:</strong> <span class="cia-badge ia-{{ a.availability }}">{{ a.availability }}</span></td>
        <td><strong>RAA:</strong> {{ raa_badge(a.raa) }}</td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    {% if a.description %}<p>{{ a.description }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="out-of-scope-assets" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Out of Scope Assets</h2>
  {% if out_of_scope_assets %}
  <p>This section lists the assets excluded from the threat model's accreditation boundary, with the
  justification for each.</p>
  {% for a in out_of_scope_assets %}
  <h2>{{ a.title }}</h2>
  <p>{{ a.justification_out_of_scope }}</p>
  {% endfor %}
  {% else %}
  <p>No technical assets in this model are marked out of scope.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section id="trust-boundaries" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Trust Boundaries</h2>
  <p>This section lists every network, cluster, and namespace boundary in the model, nested to match
  the architecture, with its tags and technical assets.</p>
  {% macro boundary(b, depth=0) %}
  <div class="boundary-node" style="margin-left: {{ depth * 20 }}px;">
    <h3>{{ b.title }} <span class="boundary-type">({{ b.type }})</span></h3>
    <p>{{ b.description }}</p>
    {% if b.tags %}<p class="tag-list">{% for t in b.tags %}<code>{{ t }}</code> {% endfor %}</p>{% endif %}
    {% if b.assets %}<p><strong>Assets inside:</strong> {{ b.assets | join(', ') }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% for child in b.children %}{{ boundary(child, depth + 1) }}{% endfor %}
  {% endmacro %}
  {% for root in trust_boundary_tree %}{{ boundary(root) }}{% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="shared-runtimes" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Shared Runtimes</h2>
  <p>This section lists the compute platforms, such as a shared Kubernetes cluster, that host several
  technical assets that do not otherwise share a trust boundary. Thus, it shows the blast radius if
  the platform itself is compromised.</p>
  {% for rt in shared_runtimes %}
  <div class="runtime-node">
    <h3>{{ rt.title }}</h3>
    <p>{{ rt.description }}</p>
    {% if rt.tags %}<p class="tag-list">{% for t in rt.tags %}<code>{{ t }}</code> {% endfor %}</p>{% endif %}
    {% if rt.assets %}<p><strong>Assets running:</strong> {{ rt.assets | join(', ') }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="disclaimer" style="page: content;">
  <h2 class="section-heading">Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>This report was generated by an automated threat-modeling process (Threagile, extended with a
  custom risk-injection engine), and it is a point-in-time analysis of the architecture as modeled.
  It supports, but does not replace, manual security review, penetration testing, and continuous
  monitoring. Thus, identified risks should be triaged and tracked to resolution through the
  organization's standard risk-management process.</p>
</section>

</body>
</html>
